WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:02.039
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:07.379
A rectangle is divided into four rectangles with the following areas:

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:16.300
The yellow rectangle has an area of 16, the blue rectangle has an area of 13 and the green rectangle has an area of 39.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.600
What is the area of the orange rectangle?

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:26.940
Can you figure it out? Give this problem to try and when you're ready keep watching the video or the solution!

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:44.060
You could solve this problem by setting up variables and then eventually solving for the area of the unknown rectangle.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:48.020
But there is a geometric principle that will make the problem a lot easier.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:54.100
First, notice that the green and the blue rectangle share the same height.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:01:01.800
This means we can figure out the width of the green rectangle relative to the width of the blue rectangle.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:09.040
Because the area of the green rectangle is 3 times the area of the blue rectangle,

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:15.020
this means the blue rectangle fits exactly 3 times into the green rectangle.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:20.009
The green rectangle has the width that is 3 times the blue rectangle.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:28.780
This means the orange rectangle has the width that is 3 times that of the yellow rectangle.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:34.360
So the yellow rectangle will fit exactly 3 times into the orange rectangle.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:43.280
Therefore, the area of the orange rectangle will be 3 times that of 16 which is 48.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.400
Did you figure this out?

